    {
      "id": "claim_87a623a265184351bb5337be2fcbc9f5",
      "statement": "RuuviTag Gas's Phase 2a hardware design gates both the HX711 and the load-cell bridge with a high-side P-MOSFET (Q2) driven by an N-MOSFET (Q1) tied to GPIO HX711_EN (P0.03), so the circuit draws effectively zero current when idle, deliberately differing from GasBee nRF's permanently-on 3V3-rail HX711 supply because RuuviTag Gas is powered from a CR2477 coin cell rather than USB/LiPo.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://hardware/schematics/ruuvitag_gas/PHASE2_HX711.md#L59-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f249534f35b6ba334ac7d83ff7bcd4503b74b6a8c3624ccb7a5b465ad0be8ffa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4a301a73ab6a4c499386ca05a586a585",
      "statement": "The Schaudt LT 45X control panel is required for the EBL 262-3 power-distribution unit to operate at all (the EBL manual states its control inputs are driven exclusively by the attached LT/IT panel), and the panel connects to the EBL over Molex Micro-Fit headers whose 12V-Ein/12V-Aus pulse inputs drive the EBL's internal bistable high-side relay, alongside Netzkontrolle, battery-fühler, and Multimedia signal pins.",
